  "sentences": [
    {
      "turn": "S1",
      "sentence": "The four core functions of the NIST AI RMF are **GOVERN, MAP, MEASURE,** and **MANAGE**.",
      "keys": [
        "C1",
        "C2"
      ],
      "positive": 0.9998,
      "negatives": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "genai_profile:genai_action_table:0075:2",
          "score": 0.0108
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "genai_profile:footnote:0008:1",
          "score": 0.0014
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "genai_profile:prose:0080:2",
          "score": 0.046
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": "S2",
      "sentence": "The AI RMF defines trustworthy AI systems as those that exhibit the following characteristics: “valid and reliable,” “safe,” “secure and resilient,” “accountable and transparent,” “explainable and interpretable,” “privacy‑enhanced,” and “fair with harmful bias managed”.",
      "keys": [
        "C1",
        "C2"
      ],
      "positive": 0.9999,
      "negatives": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "ai_rmf_1_0:prose:0020:2",
          "score": 0.3551
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "ai_rmf_1_0:prose:0049:1",
          "score": 0.6922
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "genai_profile:genai_action_table:0052:2",
          "score": 0.1034
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": "S2",
      "sentence": "Valid & Reliable is identified as a necessary condition for trustworthiness, forming the base for the other characteristics.",
      "keys": [
        "C4"
      ],
      "positive": 0.9985,
      "negatives": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "genai_profile:genai_action_table:0068:1",
          "score": 0.0012
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "ai_rmf_1_0:rmf_core_table:0044:1",
          "score": 0.0
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "ai_rmf_1_0:rmf_core_table:0037:1",
          "score": 0.043
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": "S4",
      "sentence": "It also includes outputs that diverge from the prompts or other input or that contradict previously generated statements in the same context, and is colloquially referred to as “hallucinations” or “fabrications”.",
      "keys": [
        "C1"
      ],
      "positive": 1.0,
      "negatives": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "genai_profile:prose:0020:2",
          "score": 0.0052
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "ai_rmf_1_0:prose:0000:3",
          "score": 0.0
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "genai_profile:footnote:0006:1",
          "score": 0.4247
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": "S4",
      "sentence": "GAI outputs may further contain confabulated logic or citations that purport to justify the answer, potentially misleading humans into inappropriately trusting the system’s output.",
      "keys": [
        "C3"
      ],
      "positive": 0.9999,
      "negatives": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "ai_rmf_1_0:prose:0017:1",
          "score": 0.0012
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "ai_rmf_1_0:figure:0009:1",
          "score": 0.0005
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "genai_profile:prose:0023:1",
          "score": 0.0123
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": "S5",
      "sentence": "The Generative AI Profile recommends that organizations put in place protocols that allow GAI systems to be deactivated when necessary and that, when decommissioning, they consider factors such as data‑retention requirements, data security and leakage, dependencies with other systems, use of open‑source data or models, and users’ emotional entanglement with the GAI functions.",
      "keys": [
        "C1"
      ],
      "positive": 0.9902,
      "negatives": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "genai_profile:prose:0086:2",
          "score": 0.0048
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "ai_rmf_1_0:rmf_core_table:0033:1",
          "score": 0.0054
        },
        {
          "chunk_id": "genai_profile:prose:0015:1",
          "score": 0.0203
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "turn": "S5",
      "sentence": "It also advises establishing policies, procedures and oversight functions that span the entire GAI lifecycle, from problem formulation and supply chains to system decommission, to ensure safe and risk‑aware phasing out of GAI systems.",
      "keys": [
        "C2"
      ],
      "positive": 0.9434,
      "negatives": [
        {
          "chunk_id": "ai_rmf_1_0:rmf_core_table:0026:1",
          "score": 0.006
